; Jump jet, worn on the back. See jump_jet.gd: it is carried rather than held,
; so unlike everything else in the catalogue it has no sights, no trigger and no
; grip markers -- nothing here is ever seen in a pair of hands.
;
; Two tanks on a back plate with a nozzle under each, canted out a few degrees
; so the exhaust clears the wearer's legs. Each nozzle carries two emitters: a
; short bright flame that lives a tenth of a second, and a slower smoke that
; outlives it and drifts. Both together, because a flame on its own reads as a
; sparkler and smoke on its own reads as a fault.
[gd_scene load_steps=17 format=3]

